            "bug_id": 19227,
            "text": "The numeric ALTREP Elt methods (behind INTEGER_ELT(), REAL_ELT(), ...), and Get_region, Is_sorted, No_NA and Dataptr_or_null, run with the garbage collector enabled, while R's own C code reads unprotected values through these accessors: asReal(eval(fn, rho)) in nlminb(), asRbool() on the result of chooseOpsMethod(), asInteger(eval(...)) in forceAndCall(). A package class whose Elt method allocates can therefore have its object collected while its own method runs.\n\nThis came up on R-devel in 2021 (\"Possible ALTREP bug\", https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-devel/2021-May/080793.html): Luke Tierney said integer and real Elt methods \"are not expected to allocate\", and Jim Hester noted that GC is not suspended for them \"primarily due to performance concerns\". The rule is not in Writing R Extensions, and the ALTREP design notes say the opposite (\"Operations REAL_ELT, REAL_GET_RANGE and the like may also allocate, but ... code written or modified to use them should take this into account\").\n\nReproducible example:\n\ngcaltrep.c (attached) defines an ALTREP class that wraps an ordinary vector and allocates in every method; altrep-gc-repro.R (attached) runs three calls under gctorture2(1, inhibit_release = TRUE), with a user function returning a fresh object of that class:\n\n  structure(1, class = \"a\") + structure(1, class = \"b\")   # chooseOpsMethod.a() returns one\n  nlminb(c(1, 2), function(p) alt(sum(p^2)))\n  forceAndCall(alt(1L), function(x) x, 7)\n\nOn an --enable-strict-barrier build of R-devel r90650 all three fail with \"unprotected object (0x...) encountered\" (was LGLSXP / REALSXP / INTSXP); expected \"a\", ~0 and 7. The same calls returning ordinary values are clean, as are 15 similar call sites (optim, optimize, uniroot, vapply, if/while conditions, ...) that root the value before reading it.\n\nTwo candidate patches, against r90684; either one settles it:\n\n1. altrep-methods-doc.diff documents the rule in Writing R Extensions: which methods run with GC suspended (Dataptr, string/list Elt/Set_elt), and that the numeric Elt, Get_region, Is_sorted, No_NA and Dataptr_or_null methods should neither allocate nor signal errors (an error jump is the other assumption these call sites make). Also https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/386.\n\n2. altrep-methods-gc-disabled.diff suspends GC in src/main/altrep.c around those dispatches too, as is already done for Dataptr and the string/list Elt methods, so allocating in these methods becomes safe at every call site. The cost is one flag save/restore per ALTREP method call: a for loop over seq_len(1e7) goes from about 0.085 to 0.088 s, and region-based paths are unchanged. It does not help with errors signalled from a method. make check passes. Also https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/385, where CI results can be seen.",
